<item><title>Djibouti assigns 104 public buildings to fibre programme</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/djibouti-assigns-104-public-buildings-to-fibre-programme-93b831/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/djibouti-assigns-104-public-buildings-to-fibre-programme-93b831/</guid><category>Djibouti</category><description>The operational phase covers mainly administrative buildings, schools and health centres, with the government aiming to finish by December 2026.</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:53:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/djibouti-assigns-104-public-buildings-to-fibre-programme-93b831/share.jpg" length="40403" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/djibouti-assigns-104-public-buildings-to-fibre-programme-93b831/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Djibouti seeks second term leading Indian Ocean youth and sports commission</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/djibouti-seeks-second-term-leading-indian-ocean-youth-and-3d0f8d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/djibouti-seeks-second-term-leading-indian-ocean-youth-and-3d0f8d/</guid><category>Djibouti</category><description>The country, currently holding the presidency, declared its candidacy as ministers met in Djibouti City to assess programmes and regional cooperation.</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:01:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dj.jpg" length="31696" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dj.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Djibouti researcher publishes regional food-security book</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/djibouti-researcher-publishes-regional-food-security-book-e64a49/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/djibouti-researcher-publishes-regional-food-security-book-e64a49/</guid><category>Djibouti</category><description>The 274-page study sets out field-based approaches to degraded land, irrigation and heat-resistant seeds for Djibouti and the Horn of Africa.</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:19:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dj.jpg" length="31696" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dj.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Djibouti’s carbon-quota registry draws interest from African countries</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/djibouti-s-carbon-quota-registry-draws-interest-from-7fbcc3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/djibouti-s-carbon-quota-registry-draws-interest-from-7fbcc3/</guid><category>Djibouti</category><description>The sovereign emissions-trading system, Africa’s first, was introduced three years ago as global shipping operators lag on carbon pricing.</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:47:04 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dj.jpg" length="31696" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dj.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
